{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Who turns</b> — for He dries up the waters of the sea and the Jordan, and the moist waters, and brings forth streams, which are moist, from the rock, which is dry. Also the vav is added to its meaning [as a conjunction]. And behold, the meaning: for HaShem alone does a thing and its opposite, and behold the sea and the Jordan and the rocks — He split them and reversed their nature."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 114, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:39.335989080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}